    "question": "Alex gets paid $500 a week and 10% of his weekly income is deducted as tax. He also pays his weekly water bill for $55 and gives away another 10% of his weekly income as a tithe. How much money does Alex have left?",
    "gold": "345",
    "answer": "His income tax is 10% of 500 which is 500*10% = $<<500*10*.01=50>>50.\nHis tithe costs 10% of $500 which is 500*10% = $<<500*10*.01=50>>50.\nThe total expenses are 50 + 55 + 50 = $155\nHe is then left with $500 - $ 155= $<<500-155=345>>345.\n#### 345"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much money Alex has left after deductions, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the tax deduction.\n2. Calculate the tithe deduction.\n3. Subtract the tax and tithe from Alex's weekly income.\n4. Subtract the weekly water bill from the remaining amount.\n\nLet's start with the tax deduction. Alex's weekly income is $500, and 10% of his income is deducted as tax:\n\\[\n\\text{Tax deduction} = 0.10 \\times 500 = 50\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the tithe deduction. Alex gives away 10% of his weekly income as a tithe:\n\\[\n\\text{Tithe deduction} = 0.10 \\times 500 = 50\n\\]\n\nNow, we subtract the tax and tithe from Alex's weekly income:\n\\[\n\\text{Remaining amount after tax and tithe} = 500 - 50 - 50 = 400\n\\]\n\nFinally, we subtract the weekly water bill from the remaining amount:\n\\[\n\\text{Remaining amount after water bill} = 400 - 55 = 345\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the amount of money Alex has left is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{345}\n\\]",
